.Dd $Mdocdate: May 16 2026 $
.Dt UXMPP 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm uxmpp
.Nd Unix Style XMPP Utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cm Generic Form:
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl f
.Op Fl i Ar in_fifo
.Op Fl j Ar user_jid
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl n Ar nickname
.Op Fl o Ar out_fifo
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Op Fl t Ar target_jid
.Op Fl u Ar u_seconds
.Op Fl v
.Cm COMMAND
.Pp
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl j Ar user_jid
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Fl t Ar target_jid
.Cm disco
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl i Ar in_fifo
.Op Fl j Ar user_jid
.Op Fl m
.Op Fl n Ar nickname
.Op Fl o Ar out_fifo
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Fl t Ar target_jid
.Op Fl u Ar u_seconds
.Cm bot
.Nm
.Op Fl d
.Op Fl j Ar user_jid
.Op Fl p Ar password
.Fl t Ar target_jid
.Cm ping
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
consists of a set of tools for querying, testing, configuring, 
troubleshooting, and generally using XMPP services in a UNIX way.
Many functions and utilities require an existing c2s
connection in order to facilitate tasks. The
.Fl j ,
or it's corresponding environment variable
.Ev XMPP_JID
are thus typically required.
.Pp
.Ss COMMAND must be one of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm disco
Perform a host disco(very) on
.Ar target_jid
using a
.Ar user_jid
corresponding to an active user JID of the target host or of another provider
that may federate with the target host.
.It Cm bot
Connect to a given provider, join a MUC, and handle stanzas. Optionally
if one of
.Fl f ,
.Fl i ,
and or
.Fl o
is given, fifo's corresponding to input and output
of the applicable bot are created.  These may be used to script bot
behavior using any language or tools desired. NOTE: if an
.Fl o Ar output_fifo
is specified the bot will hang, and not process stanzas until the the
applicable
.Ar output_fifo
is read.
.It Cm ping
Send an xmpp:ping to the applicable
.Ar target_jid .
.El
.Ss The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl d
Enable debug messages to stderr
.It Fl f
Enable in/out FIFOs for the applicable bot's connection.
.It Fl i Ar input_path
Specify an input path. If used with the
.Cm bot
command, data written to the specified fifo will be read by uxmpp and
passed on to the running bot.
.It Fl j Ar user_jid
Specify a user JID. Certain actions, such as the
.Cm disco
command, require s2s connections that are made on behalf of the
applicable
.Ar user_jid .
The password may be provided at the subsequent prompt (best option). If
you like to live dangerously however, you may do so by setting the
.Ev XMPP_PASSWORD
environment variable, or by supplying the password via the
.Fl p
option.
.It Fl m
If used with the
.Cm bot
command, enables default responses.
.It Fl n Ar nickname
Specify a nickname to use when joining a channel, default is the node of
the corresponding
.Ar user_jid .
.It Fl o Ar output_path
Specify an output path. If used with the
.Cm bot
command, this specifies the fifo that messages from the applicable MUC
will be written to.
.It Fl p Ar password
Specify a password. You should know it is widely accepted as a bad idea to
provide credentials in this manner; I would certainly raise an eyebrow if a
person used this option corresponding to a JID with privileges. That said, you
do you.
.It Fl t Ar target_jid
Provide a target host/JID for a given function. For example:
.Cm xmpp.example.com .
.It Fl u Ar u_seconds
Specify a value in microseconds. The
.Cm bot
command for example periodically pings the server to keep the corresponding
TCP connection alive, this value is used as the ping interval.
.It Fl v
Print version and exit. Use
.Fl d
to show more detail.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev XMPP_JID
If set, this value will be used as the
.Ar user_jid .
If the
.Fl j
option is specified, this is ignored.
.It Ev XMPP_PASSWORD
If set this value will be used during authentication. 
.Pp
CAUTION:
It is exceedingly easy for other programs running in your environment to read 
this variable thus: like the
.Fl p
option, this should only be used in special cases.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Rs
libstrophe XMPP client library:
https://strophe.im
.El
